name: sim.loadImage
description: Loads an image from file or memory
luaSynopsis: bytes image, list resolution = sim.loadImage(int options, string/bytes filenameOrBuffer)
pythonSynopsis: buffer image, int[2] resolution = sim.loadImage(int options, string/buffer filenameOrBuffer)
inputs:
1. options: bit-coded:
    - bit0 is set (1): the returned image is rgba, otherwise it is rgb
2. filenameOrBuffer: name of the file to read. The file extension indicates the format. To load an image from a buffer, simply prefix the buffer with "@mem"
outputs:
1. image: buffer containing the image data
2. resolution: the image resolution
replacedBy:
- name: loadImage, class: app, file: app_loadImage.method
- name: loadImageFromBuffer, class: app, file: app_loadImageFromBuffer.method
